Z||000000||FieroSTETZ||03-15-2001||12:06 AM||||in the past 3 days i saw 19 fieros! went from oceanside to magic mountain, torrance CA to see my friend's band play (rubberneck is a cool band!) went to knotts berry farm, and universal studios... there were 5 in the parking lot at knotts berry farm, all in one row side by side.. club thing maybe.. its a bummer cuz i don't have my car right now (waiting for a response from c m west as far as a new engine goes) so i was in a little blue sentra SER (pretty quick car actually) i was just surprised be the number of maroon fieros in torrance, also<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1012904&a=7460757&p=25516673&Sequence=0&res=high"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Sleeper||03-15-2001||01:22 AM||||i live in Torrance....rubberneck? i've heard of them, punk band right? torrance does have alot of fieros though but mostly 4cyl. and most are buckets cuz the ppl don't take care of them. there are some nice 6's around here but i only see every so offen like on weekends.  every once in a while one owner will stop me at the store or at work and ask me about performance parts so i'll give them a West Coast Fiero card, but most of the time i know they won't call Chris, west coast fiero owners just don't seem to be into it like the east coast ones are.  <p>[This message has been edited by Sleeper (edited 03-15-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||WKDFIRO||03-15-2001||02:06 AM||||Wow you can say that again about east coast club participation...<P>Chris West is the activities coordinator for Fieros West (we were West before Chris came to us with his name! lol) and we see a lot of nice Fieros out there and even have a lot of nice Fieros in the club but its like pulling teeth to get anyone out to a show or a run...<P>Over 60 members pay their dues but we might get 3 to come out and play...huh? <P>Still trying to figure that out...hmmmmm...maybe through this Forum we can get some people who actually want to drive their Fieros!<P>What do you think Chris and Eric?||||reg||3
Z||000003||FieroSTETZ||03-15-2001||03:10 AM||||eric and chris are cool, helping me find a new engine- don't have the time to rebuild right now and i have a partially built 3.4 tdc- but my engine went in my daily driver... rubberneck is a punk band, play a lot around torrance at clubs, skater hangouts, garages, wherever. i saw a few cool cars around torrance, a ferrari 360! was looking for used cars there, found a 1977 celica GT (one of my all time favorites!) and a charger 383 w/4spd pistol grip.. its a cool city! just wierd with that huge park in the middle (golf course, whatever) how far is cheis west's from torrance?<BR><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1012904&a=7460757&p=25516673&Sequence=0&res=high"> ||||reg||1
